        "mission_intent": "We need to develop a comprehensive Verification Process specification for the SecureEdge platform, aligned with the systems security engineering framework described in NIST SP 800-160 Volume 1. The specification must define how our verification activities will produce sufficient evidence demonstrating that SecureEdge satisfies all allocated security requirements and security characteristics at the assurance level designated for the system. Critically, the spec needs to address the fundamental security characteristic that the system exhibits only specified behaviors, interactions, and outcomes \u2014 which means our verification approach must include methods for demonstrating the absence of unspecified behaviors, not just the presence of desired ones. Reference the applicable controls from the Verification process activities in ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288 Section 6.4.8.3 and incorporate assurance case structures consistent with ISO/IEC 15026. The specification should also address how verification evidence feeds into the Information Management process for appropriate handling and stakeholder distribution, and should cross-reference our existing risk management activities under NIST SP 800-37. Please ensure the document covers verification criteria, methods of evidence collection, traceability to security requirements, assurance level justification, and the roles responsible for verification judgment. We need a draft ready for the engineering review board by end of next sprint.",
